WEBVTT

special-03-1
00:00:04.300 --> 00:00:07.590
“But the bride price? Not a penny less.”

special-03-2
00:00:07.590 --> 00:00:12.870
That is not feminism. That is putting a
price on yourself.

special-03-3
00:00:14.170 --> 00:00:19.820
Special episode: You cannot accept bride
price and claim feminism.

special-03-4
00:00:21.020 --> 00:00:24.270
Imagine two families sitting down to
negotiate the bride price.

special-03-5
00:00:24.270 --> 00:00:27.560
“We've raised our daughter for over
twenty years.”

special-03-6
00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:32.670
“This amount shows our family's
sincerity.”

special-03-7
00:00:32.670 --> 00:00:38.228
They discuss money; she is what they
discuss. She never speaks. She is not a

special-03-8
00:00:38.228 --> 00:00:42.250
party to this transaction. She is what is
being traded.

special-03-9
00:00:43.350 --> 00:00:47.900
First cut: this is a purchase. If bride
price is “compensation,” what is being

special-03-10
00:00:47.900 --> 00:00:48.600
compensated?

special-03-11
00:00:48.600 --> 00:00:52.100
“Raised for over twenty years”: the cost
of raising her, settled.

special-03-12
00:00:52.100 --> 00:00:56.220
“A daughter married out”: belonging
transfers from one family to another.

special-03-13
00:00:56.220 --> 00:00:59.710
“Give us a grandson soon”: her
childbearing belongs to his family.

special-03-14
00:00:59.710 --> 00:01:04.660
Together, this is a transfer contract:
her family gets the money; his family

special-03-15
00:01:04.660 --> 00:01:07.460
gets her labor, childbearing and
belonging.

special-03-16
00:01:07.460 --> 00:01:10.107
Gayle Rubin, “The Traffic in Women”
(1975): in Lévi-Strauss's kinship

special-03-17
00:01:10.107 --> 00:01:12.946
systems, women are exchanged objects. The
relationship forms between those

special-03-18
00:01:12.946 --> 00:01:14.020
exchanging her. (Paraphrase)

special-03-19
00:01:15.120 --> 00:01:20.158
Second cut: this is employment. The
payment buys an entitlement that can be

special-03-20
00:01:20.158 --> 00:01:21.770
claimed again and again.

special-03-21
00:01:21.770 --> 00:01:25.500
“We paid the bride price. Of course we'll
spend New Year with my family.”

special-03-22
00:01:25.500 --> 00:01:30.230
“Our family paid for you. You should be
considerate.”

special-03-23
00:01:30.230 --> 00:01:36.001
The hierarchy need not be spoken. First
it is written as a number. Every later

special-03-24
00:01:36.001 --> 00:01:38.590
“be considerate” collects interest.

special-03-25
00:01:38.590 --> 00:01:41.580
Carole Pateman, The Sexual Contract
(1988): marriage appears to be a contract

special-03-26
00:01:41.580 --> 00:01:44.414
between equals, but establishes male
domination and female subordination.

special-03-27
00:01:44.414 --> 00:01:44.880
(Paraphrase)

special-03-28
00:01:45.980 --> 00:01:50.000
Third cut: this is objectification.

special-03-29
00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:53.995
Education adds value, age subtracts it;
local household registration adds value,

special-03-30
00:01:53.995 --> 00:01:57.790
remarriage subtracts it. A whole person
becomes a list of priced attributes.

special-03-31
00:01:57.790 --> 00:02:04.330
However high the price, it still says
only that she is a valuable object.

special-03-32
00:02:05.430 --> 00:02:11.740
Now look at that “feminist's” checklist.

special-03-33
00:02:11.740 --> 00:02:18.130
Reject every tradition that costs you.
Accept every tradition that benefits you.

special-03-34
00:02:18.130 --> 00:02:23.226
But they belong to the same system. Bride
price pays for the daughter likened to

special-03-35
00:02:23.226 --> 00:02:28.130
“water poured away.” You cannot reject
the bill but accept the sale proceeds.

special-03-36
00:02:29.230 --> 00:02:36.097
Episode 1 asked: how radical you are
depends on which relationships you seek

special-03-37
00:02:36.097 --> 00:02:37.000
to change.

special-03-38
00:02:37.000 --> 00:02:41.411
What relationship changes when you
negotiate a higher bride price? None.

special-03-39
00:02:41.411 --> 00:02:42.820
Only the price changes.

special-03-40
00:02:42.820 --> 00:02:50.545
When you bargain over your own price, you
have already accepted that you can be

special-03-41
00:02:50.545 --> 00:02:51.230
priced.

special-03-42
00:02:52.330 --> 00:02:55.790
Let's examine four common defenses, one
by one.

special-03-43
00:02:55.790 --> 00:02:58.660
“Bride price gives women security.”

special-03-44
00:02:58.660 --> 00:03:02.877
Security should come from income,
property and law, not a buyer's one-off

special-03-45
00:03:02.877 --> 00:03:07.152
payment. Relying on it for “security”
accepts that you are the party whose

special-03-46
00:03:07.152 --> 00:03:10.560
value depreciates. That is exactly what
must be overturned.

special-03-47
00:03:10.560 --> 00:03:13.880
“The money isn't mine. It goes to my
parents.”

special-03-48
00:03:13.880 --> 00:03:18.810
Then it is worse: the parents make the
deal. You are not even the seller. You

special-03-49
00:03:18.810 --> 00:03:20.410
are what is being traded.

special-03-50
00:03:20.410 --> 00:03:23.730
“The groom's side wants a house and car
too. That's reciprocity.”

special-03-51
00:03:23.730 --> 00:03:27.335
Demands in both directions are not
equality. They are pricing in both

special-03-52
00:03:27.335 --> 00:03:27.910
directions.

special-03-53
00:03:27.910 --> 00:03:30.810
“It's our custom. I respect my parents.”

special-03-54
00:03:30.810 --> 00:03:35.595
Feminism never requires respect for
oppressive customs. “Respect” and “being

special-03-55
00:03:35.595 --> 00:03:38.680
considerate” are this system's most
useful words.

special-03-56
00:03:38.680 --> 00:03:44.644
In the comments: what is the most
self-righteous justification for taking

special-03-57
00:03:44.644 --> 00:03:46.850
bride price you have heard?

special-03-58
00:03:47.950 --> 00:03:51.830
Don't call this overpoliticizing. Look at
what the law says.

special-03-59
00:03:51.830 --> 00:03:55.713
The Civil Code prohibits marriage by
purchase and demanding money or property

special-03-60
00:03:55.713 --> 00:03:56.570
through marriage.

special-03-61
00:03:56.570 --> 00:04:00.914
Article 5: if cohabitation was brief and
bride price excessive, consider

special-03-62
00:04:00.914 --> 00:04:05.680
cohabitation, pregnancy and childbirth in
deciding whether it must be returned.

special-03-63
00:04:05.680 --> 00:04:09.722
Whether to return it, and how much,
depends on how long you lived together

special-03-64
00:04:09.722 --> 00:04:13.709
and whether there was pregnancy or
childbirth. What does money settled by

special-03-65
00:04:13.709 --> 00:04:16.440
“how long she stayed, whether she gave
birth” buy?

special-03-66
00:04:16.440 --> 00:04:19.059
Civil Code, Article 1042; Supreme
People's Court provisions on bride price,

special-03-67
00:04:19.059 --> 00:04:20.630
effective February 1, 2024, Articles 5
and 6.

special-03-68
00:04:21.830 --> 00:04:24.220
Let's be clear who is being condemned.

special-03-69
00:04:24.220 --> 00:04:28.705
Girls whose parents decide for them, and
who cannot refuse, are the objects of

special-03-70
00:04:28.705 --> 00:04:30.660
this transaction, not the accused.

special-03-71
00:04:30.660 --> 00:04:35.569
The accused are those who set the price,
accept the payment and then invoke

special-03-72
00:04:35.569 --> 00:04:37.140
“feminism” to defend it.

special-03-73
00:04:37.140 --> 00:04:42.200
Such people have no right to invoke
feminism.

special-03-74
00:04:43.300 --> 00:04:47.740
Feminism is not about getting a good
price for yourself.

special-03-75
00:04:47.740 --> 00:04:52.370
It is about no longer having a price.

special-03-76
00:04:54.670 --> 00:04:59.570
This is UjiBricks.
